# Secrets Management

- Never commit secrets, put them in public env prefixes (`NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, `VITE_*`, etc.), or log them.
- `.env` gitignored; `.env.example` names + dummies only.
- Load/validate config at boot (fail fast); centralize env access; fake values in fixtures.
- On leak: rotate keys—do not only rewrite git history.
- Prefer secret scanning in hooks/CI (e.g. gitleaks).

Korean rationale: `docs/pvc-guide/ko/security/secret-management.md`
